I got off the train at Lonavala station.
The air outside was very different.
Mumbai's heat was not here.
I immediately felt a refreshing coolness.
I picked up my backpack and put it on my shoulders.
The platform was very crowded.
Many people were picking up their own luggage.
I walked slowly towards the exit.
Just then, I saw a stall on the platform.
A man was selling Lonavala's famous chikki there.
I went near his stall.
I looked at his colorful packets.
"Bhaiya, give me one packet of peanut chikki," I said.
He smiled and gave me a packet.
"This is very fresh, madam," he said.
I took my wallet out of my pocket.
The price was fifty rupees.
I gave him fifty rupees.
Then I put that chikki in my bag.
Now I was ready for my walk.
